Hints
Each call to hint gives the next rung of the ladder. After the last rung, it gives the last hint again.



hint
def hint(
    qid:str
)-&gt;str:
The next hint on the ladder, from the least to the most revealing.


A board of the screen guide on an open check counts as one hint, as a hint from the ladder does: board_hint keeps the words of the board as the next hint, with via='board', and gives the count of hints. When the ladder is used up, it keeps nothing and gives None.



board_hint
def board_hint(
    qid:str, text:str
)-&gt;int | None:
Count the board that explained open question qid as its next hint, with text as its words. The count of hints now, or None when the ladder is used up.

Related topics
related gives the concepts next to slug in the graph. First come the concepts that build on it, then the related ones, then its prereqs. The concepts that are not learned come first. with_step finds the walks that have a concept. beyond gives what comes after a walk: the concepts that build on its steps and are not in it.


